","default":false,"description":"PR fully implemented spawning issue","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-11-08T10:23:00Z","updated_at":"2026-11-25T02:53:54Z","closed_at":"2026-11-08T10:23:28Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7635","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7635","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7635.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7635.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-08T10:23:28Z"},"body":"Fixes #7075 (task 12978).\n\nDocs-only change to `pkgs/mcpx/docs/`:\n\n- `mcp.md`: after the `?codemode=false` switch paragraph, a concrete opencode v2 example — a remote mcpx server entry (`http://127.0.0.1:8899/mcp`) with `codemode: false` — explaining that with the opt-out set, v2 leaves mcpx's gateway tools in the model's direct tool list and does not append the parameter, and that the same field exists on a local (stdio) entry.\n- `plugins.md`: the stale v2 caveat (\"whether v2's code-mode defaults recognise mcpx and turn that off for it is unknown\") is corrected to the documented behaviour (PLG-35): v2 does not recognise mcpx automatically; for a remote server it appends `?codemode=false` so its own code mode can orchestrate the pooled servers, and `codemode: false` in the v2 `mcp` config is the opt-out.\n\nVerification (packet tests):\n- `grep codemode pkgs/mcpx/docs/plugins.md` → corrected caveat present (2 hits; `mcp.md` 6 hits including the example).\n- The stale \"recognise mcpx and turn that off for it is unknown\" text returns nothing.\n\nNo code behaviour changes.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796725383&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7635&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7635&signature=c4ccf84f0c6b5a7d54f2bf566dc6d42ce0e5f8268d55d6a7218775cd12c0250d\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7635?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7635/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7635/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/8089","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/8089/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/8089/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/8089/events","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/8089","id":6297824341,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABN_UGYg","number":8089,"title":"mcpx(plugin): thread host abort signal through mcpx_exec (PLG-38, #1940)","user":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2026-11-10T00:52:44Z","updated_at":"2026-11-10T06:35:26Z","closed_at":"2026-11-10T06:35:23Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/8089","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/8089","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/8089.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/8089.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-10T06:35:23Z"},"body":"Queue task 13061, issue #1940 remainder.\n\nPLG-38: mcpx_exec ignored the host abort signal, so an aborted session blocked to completion. This threads ToolContext.abort through both paths:\n- Daemon path: DaemonClient.exec(source, session, signal) forwards the signal as CallOptions.signal to the generated daemon client, cancelling the in-flight /v1/exec request.\n- CLI fallback: viaCLI/runBin accept the signal; an already-aborted session never spawns the binary, and an abort mid-run kills the child and is named in the result instead of surfacing as a missing binary.\n- A daemon-path abort is caught in mcpx_exec and reported as an abort, not a daemon failure.\n\nCODE-53 needs no change here: the codemode:false user config example already landed on main in #7075 (docs/mcp.md), verified fresh this shift.\n\nTests:\n- bun test (plugin/opencode): 133 pass, 5 skip (live-daemon only), 0 fail. New: daemon-path abort against a fake daemon on a real socket (ops.test.ts), CLI-path abort plus a no-signal control (daemon.test.ts).\n- bunx tsc --noEmit: clean. biome lint on changed files: clean.\n- go test ./internal/mcpserver/ -run Codemode|CodeMode (pkgs/mcpx): pass.\n\nScope notes: the /v1 request-cancellation layer (#1864) and the v2 adapter are untouched, per the packet. #1940 should stay open if PLG-36/PLG-37 are later judged in-scope; this closes the CODE-53 + PLG-38 remainder.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796863968&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=8089&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F8089&signature=c557511b87bef9dbcdd795d230b3be2a5924db2eea2dff5acdefc1a864585e00\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/8089?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Cancelled tool requests now stop ongoing execution through either the daemon or command-line fallback, rather than continuing to run.\n  * If a request is cancelled before execution begins or while it is running, the tool now reports that it was aborted.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/8089/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/8089/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0}],"search_type":"lexical"}